.TH MOTHRIX 1 "2026" "mothrix 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mothrix \- a terminal Matrix client with a room sidebar and mouse support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mothrix
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B mothrix login
.RI [ SERVER ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-password ]
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B mothrix accounts
.br
.B mothrix logout
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR NAME ]
.br
.B mothrix dictionary
.RI [ LANGUAGE ]
.br
.B mothrix events
.RI [ ROOM ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR N ]
.br
.B mothrix pushers
.RB [ list | add
.I URL
.B \-\-app\-id
.I ID
.B \-\-pushkey
.IR KEY | remove
.B \-\-app\-id
.I ID
.B \-\-pushkey
.IR KEY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mothrix
is a Matrix client for the terminal. Rooms and people are listed on the
left, the conversation is on the right, and everything that can be done
with a key can also be clicked.
.PP
Without arguments it starts with all signed-in accounts, and asks for a
homeserver first if there is none.
.PP
New messages are announced on the desktop with
.BR notify-send ,
on Windows as toasts. In kitty the terminal shows the notifications
itself. Clicking one, in kitty or on Windows, brings the terminal to the
front with that chat open.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "login " "[SERVER]"
Sign in.
.I SERVER
is a homeserver name or address, or a full Matrix ID. Browser sign-in is
used where the server offers it;
.B \-\-password
asks for the password instead. With
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
the account is added next to the ones already there, under that name.
.TP
.B accounts
List the signed-in accounts.
.TP
.B update
Install a new release, if there is one (only the release files from
GitHub; a package says to update it with the package manager). The
release is checked against mothrix's signature first.
.TP
.B logout
Sign out and delete the account's data on this computer, including its
encryption keys. Not while another mothrix is running with the account.
.TP
.BI "dictionary " "[LANGUAGE]"
List the spell-check dictionaries, or download one (like de_DE).
.TP
.BI "events " "[ROOM]"
Show the types and structure of a room's recent events with all text
masked, for reporting what another client sends.
.TP
.B pushers
List the account's pushers: where its homeserver sends push
notifications for phones. With
.B add
or
.BR remove ,
add or remove one by hand, for trying a push gateway such as Sygnal.
Added ones ask for event ids only, never message text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " \fINAME\fR"
The account to use. When starting: only this account.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the commands and keys.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version; a build that is not a release adds the commit it was
made from (the settings dialog shows the same).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Tab
Switch between the room list and the message box.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+K ", " /
Find a room.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search messages.
.TP
.B F2
Settings (accounts, spell checking, what is shown).
.TP
.B F3
With several accounts: all of them, or one at a time.
.TP
.B F5
The emoji picker: search every emoji and put one into the message box.
.TP
.BR Alt+Up ", " Alt+Down
Previous and next room.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.PP
Typing
.B /
in the message box lists the commands available there. The full list of
keys is in
.I usage.md
with the documentation (/usr/share/doc/mothrix, or docs/ in the source).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mothrix/config.toml
Settings, your own themes and key bindings, and
.B proxy
(an HTTP proxy for every connection; else the
.B HTTPS_PROXY
or
.B ALL_PROXY
environment variable). Readable only by you.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mothrix/<profile>/
One folder per account: session, encryption keys, log.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mothrix/state.json
The room open last time and unsent drafts.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mothrix/
Attachments you opened and pictures you pasted, for a day.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOTHRIX_PASSWORD
The password for
.BR "mothrix login" ,
instead of typing it.
.TP
.B MOTHRIX_LOG
.BR debug " or " info
for a more detailed log file.
.SH BUGS
Source, issues and releases:
.UR https://github.com/r1sq/mothrix
.UE
